  "details": "Summary:\n\nBuild & Publish does nothing (no error, no upload), but Build & Test works normally.\n\nEnvironment:\n\n- OS: Windows 11\n\n- Unity: 2022.3.x LTS\n\n- VRChat Avatars SDK: latest and previous versions (both tested)\n\n- Account: Trusted User (account age ~2 years)\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1. Create a new Avatars project via VRChat Creator Companion\n\n2. Add Avatars SDK\n\n3. Open project in Unity\n\n4. Login via SDK Control Panel\n\n5. Click \"Build & Publish\"\n\n6. Nothing happens (UI locks partially, no error, no upload)\n\nExpected Result:\n\nAvatar should be uploaded and publish dialog should appear.\n\nActual Result:\n\nNothing happens. No error message is shown.\n\nBuild & Test works normally.\n\nNotes:\n\n- Issue reproduces even in a brand new project\n\n- Windows was fully reset via cloud reinstall\n\n- Unity, SDK, and GPU drivers were reinstalled\n\n- Network was tested via mobile tethering\n\n- Blueprint ID reset and avatar name change did not help",
